ctitious belief that someone rich or famous is in love with you.\par \par \uc2 CARTER EVANS: Less than 24 hours later, Carpenter alleges Applegate returned outside the singer`s home "watching and waiting."\par \par \uc2 The next day, she says he was there again in this silver Prius,\par \par \uc2 JEFF DUNN: See a person that has been arrested, released from custody, and returns the very next day is very persistent, and from a threat assessment perspective, that`s someone that you have to watch very closely.\par \par \uc2 (Clip from Coachella/April 2026)\par \par \uc2 CARTER EVANS: The "Espresso" singer is the latest celebrity to be targeted at home.\par \par \uc2 In March, shots were fired at Rihanna`s Beverly Hills mansion, and last year, Taylor Swift was granted a restraining order against a man she says routinely showed up and claimed she had his baby.\par \par \uc2 For CBS MORNINGS, I`m Carter Evans.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: That is scary!\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I was going to say it`s so terrifying. I`m so glad she has security, and security clearly knew what they were doing.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Yes.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: But it`s scary that he keeps on returning.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Returning.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Keeps on returning.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: That`s what I don`t understand.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Because then if somebody doesn`t get the hint one or two times --\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: -- what are they going to do on the fourth or fifth time?\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Exactly right.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: And we have to wait till something happens.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Which we don`t want.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: We just hope that doesn`t happen.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: No.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Exactly right.\par \par \uc2 All right ahead in "What to Watch": We`ve got a big announcement from Tayl