LE KING: Uh-huh.\par \par \uc2 ZAC POSEN: And that art is owned and lived by the people, not by institute.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Bravo.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Incredible.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Bravo.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: The wings are incredible. It really does!\par \par \uc2 ZAC POSEN: That was the surprising find.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: It made the moment. But getting back to the silhouette, how do you capture the contours of her body?\par \par \uc2 ZAC POSEN: Oh, well, we 3D scanned her body.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Really?\par \par \uc2 ZAC POSEN: Yes, she wanted it about her body as the sculpture so -- and then what we did is we molded a leather bustier of her body, which is here, underneath her belly button and all sown in there.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: There is so much work that gets into it.\par \par \uc2 ZAC POSEN: It has been layered. I worked with these artisanal designers. They have this great brand here in New York. They come from an Argentinian saddle leather making company and they molded this bodice that`s her under structure of her body on top of her body,\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Incredible!\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I just say, kudos to you, Zac, because everybody says you are changing the game over at Gap, because we`re seeing all the different brands people say there is a noticeable difference.\par \par \uc2 I wonder, do you still get nervous doing what you do with the track record that you have?\par \par \uc2 ZAC POSEN: Absolutely!\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Do you always feel you have to up yourself? Do you always feel that?\par \par \uc2 ZAC POSEN: I mean, I challenge myself every day.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Got it\par \par \uc2 ZAC POSEN: Right? because I like to -- I think it`s important to learn something new every day.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Yes.\par \par \uc2 ZAC POSEN: Keep your eyes and ears to the ground. Keep interested, ask questions. I mean, this is what evolves the world and evolves you.\par \par \uc2 You know, working alongside an incredible group of people, building this business, and then being able to have the opportunity to be able to take fashion as an art form at rare special culture moments with Gap Studio is really a dream come true.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Do you have any special moments at the Gala last night?\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Yes.\par \par \uc2 ZAC POSEN: Wow. I mean, there`s a few. I mean, I was in -- I got this great moment with my girl, Rihanna, in the bathroom, in the men`s room.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: In the men`s room?\par \par \uc2 ZAC POSEN: With her man, so that was really nice. You know, we go way back!\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: What were you all doing in the bathroom?\par \par \uc2 ZAC POSEN: I don`t know what they were doing. I was like, I had to go pee.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Okay!\par \par \uc2 ZAC POSEN: Like, finally, it`s like, a long evening. It`s like, okay. I was like, you know, Kendall, do you mind, I`ve got to run!\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Okay.\par \par \uc2 ZAC POSEN: And she was there, and they were just, I don`t know -- I don`t know if they were coming, gone to the bathroom, late arrival, but who knows? But it was really lovely and warm.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Any other looks stand out to you?\par \par \uc2 ZAC POSEN: Yes, there are amazing look so there`s a young woman, Emma Chamberlain.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 ZAC POSEN: Who posed this -- she was wearing this amazing dress by Mugler.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: There she is.\par \par \uc2 ZAC POSEN: I love the colorations. She`s just bright energy. She might be social, but she is so T.V. ready and lovely, and she looked gorgeous and cool.\par \par \uc2 I loved what Rihanna was wearing, and I love Sunday Rose and Nicole. I mean --\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes! Yes!\par \par \uc2 ZAC POSEN: That was a big debut for Sunday and Nicole.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: That`s her daughter