ed. No casualties were reported.\par \par \uc2 But it`s here in the Gulf that continues to be hit the hardest. This Iranian strike on a fuel tank at Dubai`s Airport has disrupted flights for a second day at one of the world`s busiest airports, and this major hit on a large oil storage facility in the UAE Fujairah saw it burn out-of-control as U.S. and Israeli forces continue to pound targets across Iran, they say at least 15,000 so far.\par \par \uc2 (Explosion)\par \par \uc2 IMTIAZ TYAB: And where day turned to night, after a strike on a police headquarters in Western Hamadan Province.\par \par \uc2 Israel is also continuing its other war on Iran`s most important proxy, the Israeli military has begun "limited and targeted ground operations" against Hezbollah in Southern Lebanon.\par \par \uc2 According to Lebanese authorities, since fighting began two weeks ago, at least 886 people, including over a hundred children have been killed and a million more displaced.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: That was Imtiaz Tyab reporting near the Strait of Hormuz.\par \par \uc2 All right, lights are slowly coming back on in Cuba this morning, after the island`s electric grid collapsed on Monday, leaving nearly the entire population of 10 million people in the dark.\par \par \uc2 Now, it is unclear what led to the blackout, which comes as the U.S. has been blocking all oil shipments from Venezuela, Cuba`s largest supplier.\par \par \uc2 President Trump said that Cuba`s government is on its last legs, and he`s ready to step in.\par \par \uc2 (Begin VT)\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP: I do believe, I`ll be the honor of -- having the honor of taking Cuba, I think, it`s a big honor, whether I free it, take it, think I can do anything I want with it.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Cuba`s president says his nation has not received a drop of fuel in three months.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: A federal judge in Boston has blocked the Trump 