: Wow!\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Caroline Polisi, thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: It`s wrong.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: All right, ahead, can A.I. help us manage our money? Or is it more trouble than it`s worth?\par \par \uc2 Jill Schlesinger is here. She is going to break it down with all of the tips that you need, and her wisdom is going to help. Stick around. This is CBS MORNINGS.\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: In today`s "Money Watch," we are talking about how technology can help manage your financial life. From budgeting to investing to saving, people are turning to artificial intelligence for help.\par \par \uc2 All right, so according to a recent survey, 66 percent of Americans say they`ve used A.I. to seek out financial advice, and that rises to 82 percent for millennials and Gen Z, that makes sense, right?\par \par \uc2 CBS News business analyst, Jill Schlesinger is here to break it down and let us know what this reality of A.I. and finances really is.\par \par \uc2 How are you doing?\par \par \uc2 JILL SCHLESINGER: I`m great.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: All right, so what are the best ways to incorporate technology in your financial life?\par \par \uc2 JILL SCHLESINGER: I think over the last 20 years, we know that tracking how you spend your money has become so much easier for technology.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: For sure.\par \par \uc2 JILL SCHLESINGER: We know that there are apps like Monarch and you need a budget, YNAB. There`s one for couples called Honeydue.\par \par \uc2 But even bank apps have gotten so much better.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: They have.\par \par \uc2 JILL SCHLESINGER: So this is the place where most financial questions start like, how much am I spending? Which then tells you, how much can I actually afford to invest? What can I put in retirement? So that`s the best place to start.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: So you have your traditional financial institutions, you have financial advisors. You also have apps. You have these influencers online, if you are young person trying to get involved in investing, it just seems like there are so many options.\par \par \uc2 JILL SCHLESINGER: Yes!\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Which, it could be like a daunting task to just pick one. What should people do if they just want to get started? They just want to get in the game?\par \par \uc2 JILL SCHLESINGER: I think that I always like to remind folks that if you just want to actually invest, use your company based retirement plan.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Okay.\par \par \uc2 JILL SCHLESINGER: That is by far the best way in. Now, there are also people who will come to me, some of them work here and they want to dabble. Someone asked me this this morning, before I came on the air, what should I do?\par \par \uc2 Well, you can go to a large investment firm, and you can buy no load or no cost index funds or exchange rated funds. You can do that.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Right.\par \par \uc2 JILL SCHLESINGER: You can have an app like Wealthfront or Betterment manage your money for you. But if you just want to play, you want to go to Robinhood, that`s fine. Gang, just make sure, whatever you`re putting in there is what you can afford to lose.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: When it comes to A.I. though, are there some downsides that people should be aware of?\par \par \uc2 JILL SCHLESINGER: I have to say that that stat kind of made me nervous, because I think A.I. can be great for general education, right? How do I read my pay stub? What`s the difference between a Roth and a traditional IRA?\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Streamline kind of my expenses.\par \par \uc2 JILL SCHLESINGER: Right, how do I do that?\par \par \uc2 But when you`re making a big decision, it is kind of scary to rely on A.I., which can hallucinate, and then --\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Say that again, that is important.\par \par \uc2 JILL SCHLESINGER: A.I. can hallucinate.\par \p