 favorite things I`ve ever done.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Can I just congratulate you in person for your nomination to the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ETHERIDGE: Yay!\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Which is about time, I said it to you when you came in. Only because one of our producers, Wendy McNeil and I were talking earlier, "How Come to My Window" is probably one of the top 20 greatest rock songs of all time.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes!\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: And so --\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ETHERIDGE: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Yes, and I would know, because I`m a big rock and roll fan.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: He plays a guitar, too. He has a band. He has a band.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ETHERIDGE: I saw him. We were talking guitar --\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Oh, okay!\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: That`s right. We saw that -- yes, yes, I saw that last pause. It`s beautiful --\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ETHERIDGE: Yes.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: But I just think it`s a long time coming. And how did you feel when you found out that you`d been nominated?\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ETHERIDGE: Well, I had been eligible for 12 years.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: That`s right.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ETHERIDGE: Not that I was counting.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: No, she is not counting.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ETHERIDGE: But --\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Was it 12?\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ETHERIDGE: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ETHERIDGE: And you know what? It`s so hard for the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame. It`s such a -- you know whose taste is it we`re talking about? Who likes this? Who likes that?\par \par \uc2 And rock and roll is so mercurial.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ETHERIDGE: And so, you can`t say in -- and I know that The Rock Hall has a hard time kind of figuring out, you know, who`s influencing what is rock and roll. Rock and roll changes.\