d the main phase of its offensive to destroy \uc2 Hamas\uc2  in Gaza`s largest city. Military officials say ground forces are moving deeper into the area.\par \par \uc2 Imtiaz Tyab is tracking all of this from London.\par \par \uc2 Imtiaz, good morning.\par \par \uc2 IMTIAZ TYAB: Nate, good morning to you.\par \par \uc2 Well, Gaza City residents have told CBS News they are being subjected to "heavy and relentless bombings as the Israeli military launches its ground invasion there and as the United Nations inquiry has found that Israel`s nearly two-year war on Gaza is in their words, a genocide.\par \par \uc2 (Begin VT)\par \par \uc2 IMTIAZ TYAB: Israel`s military has started what it has called the main step of its ground invasion of Gaza City, where tired neighborhoods have already been reduced to ruins and hundreds of thousands of Palestinians have been forced to flee.\par \par \uc2 It comes as Israeli leaders have reacted angrily to the U.N. Commission of Inquiry`s Genocide Report, denouncing it as "distorted and false."\par \par \uc2 DANIEL MERON (U.N. Israeli Ambassador): The report relies entirely on \uc2 Hamas\uc2  falsehoods, laundered and repeated by others.\par \par \uc2 IMTIAZ TYAB: Investigators found "reasonable grounds" that Israel has committed four of the five acts of genocide under the 1948 U.N. Convention.\par \par \uc2 NAVI PILLAY (U.N. Independent International Commission of Inquiry in Occupied Palestinian Territory Chair): The goal of the Israeli government is abundantly clear, as we continue to witness the destruction of Palestinians in Gaza. The Commission finds it is genocide.\par \par \uc2 IMTIAZ TYAB: The four acts Israel is accused of committing since the start of the war with \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , following the brutal 2023 October 7th attacks include, killing members of a group, causing them serious bodily and mental harm, deliberately inflicting conditions calculated to destroy the group, and preventing births.\par \par \uc2 The report not only sites the patterns of conduct by Israeli forces as evidence of "genocidal intent," but also the statements of Israeli leaders by alleging Prime Minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , President \uc2 Isaac Herzog\uc2 , and former Defense Minister Yoav Gallant, have all "incited the commission of genocide."\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 IMTIAZ TYAB: And a number of international and Israeli human rights groups and scholars have also accused Israel of genocide against Palestinians in Gaza. This, while the \uc2 International Court of Justice\uc2  is hearing a case that accuses Israeli forces of genocide, a case Israel has called wholly unfounded and based on biased and false claims -- Gayle.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Imtiaz, we thank you.\par \par \uc2 For the second time this month, President Trump says that he ordered the U.S. military to attack a boat that he says was carrying illegal drugs from Venezuela to this country.\par \par \uc2 Now Trump posted this video yesterday saying it shows a moment that the boat was destroyed, killing three people.\par \par \uc2 Charlie D`Agata covers The Pentagon for us.\par \par \uc2 Charlie, good morning to you. What can you tell us about this latest attack?\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE D`AGATA: Yes, good morning to you, Gayle.\par \par \uc2 So, this latest strike comes about two weeks after the U.S. military struck another Venezuelan boat, as you said, allegedly trafficking drugs, killing 11 people. The Trump administration has built up its presence in the Southern Caribbean over the last month, saying it is to combat the flow of illegal narcotics into the U.S.\par \par \uc2 (Begin VT)\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE D`AGATA: Video posted on President Trump`s Truth Social account shows what appears to be a stationary vessel in open water. Seconds later, an explosion leaves it engulfed in flames. The result of what Trump said was a targeted U.S. military strike against identified Venezuelan narcoterrorists on Monday morning.\\\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP: We have proof. All you have to do is look at the cargo that was -- like it is scattered all over the ocean. Big bags of cocaine and fentanyl all over the place.\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE D`AGATA: The President said, three people were killed aboard the boat. It comes just about two weeks after another U.S. strike killed eleven people aboard another vessel in international waters. Sources tell CBS News, that boat had attempted to turn back before it was repeatedly fired on.\par \par \uc2 Trump said those on board were members of the designated foreign terrorist organization, TDA or Tren de Aragua, something Venezuelan officials have denied.\par \par \uc2 Democratic Senator Adam Schiff, says he plans to challenge President Trump`s authority to carry out such strikes.\par \par \uc2 SEN. ADAM SCHIFF (D-CA): I don`t want to see us get into some war with Venezuela, because the President is just blowing ships willy-nilly out of the water.\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE D`AGATA: Venezuela`s government has been encouraging its citizens to join local militias and familiarize themselves with the use of firearms amid what it calls U.S. aggression in the region.\par \par \uc2 President Trump warned that the U.S. military operation against drug traffickers won`t be limited to suspected smugglers at sea.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP: And you know what? We`re telling the cartels right now, we`re going to be stopping them, too, when they come by land, we`re going to be stopping them the same way we stop the boats.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE D`AGATA: The U.S. also deployed F-35 fighter jets to the region after two Venezuelan F-16s came close to a U.S. Destroyer there. Democrats and some Republicans have expressed concern that the U.S. military actions in the region might violate international law -- Tony.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Charlie, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 We have got a number of developments in the investigation into Charlie 