s before his arrest last Thursday. Writing in part quote, "It was me at UVU yesterday. I`m sorry for all this."\par \par \uc2 The messages were first reported by "The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 ." \uc2 Discord\uc2  has said it hasn`t found any evidence that the suspect planned kirk`s assassination on the platform.\par \par \uc2 While no motive has been identified, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  Director said the suspect`s family and friends told investigators, he subscribed to a left wing ideology.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT J.D. VANCE: We have to talk about this incredibly destructive movement of left-wing extremism that has grown up over the last few years and I believe is part of the reason why Charlie was killed by an assassin`s bullet.\par \par \uc2 CARTER EVANS: Hosting his friend`s podcast late Monday, Vice President J.D. Vance vowed to prevent what he called festering violence on the far left, and appearing as a guest, President Trump`s Deputy chief-of-staff \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , argued Kirk`s death was the result of an organized campaign of terrorist networks, though he offered no evidence to support that claim.\par \par \uc2 STEPHEN MILLER\uc2 , (Deputy Chief-of-Staff for Policy and Homeland Security adviser): We are going to use every resource we have at the Department of Justice, Homeland Security, and throughout this government to identify, disrupt, dismantle, and destroy these networks and make America safe again for the American people.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 CARTER EVANS: Now for now, investigators say the suspected shooter is believed to have acted alone and we`re expecting to learn more about that later today in court.\par \par \uc2 Also today, \uc2 FBI\uc2  Director, Kash Patel, is expected to face questions about his agency`s handling of the case when he testifies on capitol hill -- Nate.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Carter, thank you.\par \par \uc2 There are major developments in the fight over TikTok. The Trump administration says it struck a deal with China that would stop the ban of the app, but there are still some pretty big questions over the details.\par \par \uc2 Senior business and tech correspondent, Jo Ling Kent has more.\par \par \uc2 Jo Ling, good morning.\par \par \uc2 JO LING KENT: Good morning, Nate.\par \par \uc2 Sources with knowledge of the negotiations tell CBS News, the tech giant, \uc2 Oracle\uc2 , is part of a group of companies that would allow TikTok in the U.S. to continue operating.\par \par \uc2 According to sources, the structure of the final deal is unclear, but it will include multiple firms. There`s no word on what level, though, of involvement there will be from Chinese companies, including TikTok`s parent company, ByteDance and what their role will be in the deal or who will ultimately control TikTok`s algorithm, that recommendation algorithm, that`s the key technology that serves up the videos that you see, keeping users scrolling TikTok.\par \par \uc2 All of this comes after Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said Monday, the administration and China have struck a framework deal to meet the requirements of a law that now requires TikTok to be owned by a U.S. entity or face a ban.\par \par \uc2 Oracle\uc2 `s founder and chairman, \uc2 Larry Ellison\uc2 , is an ally of President Trump and you may remember back in 2020, \uc2 Oracle\uc2  briefly reached a deal to buy TikTok, but then that fell apart. We should point out, his son, \uc2 David Ellison\uc2 , is now the owner of \uc2 CBS\uc2  through a merger combining his media company, \uc2 Skydance\uc2 , with CBS News` parent company, Paramount.\par \par \uc2 Of course, CBS News, we`ve reached out to \uc2 Oracle\uc2  executives and a White House spokesperson for comment and a TikTok spokesperson declined our multiple requests for comment -- Nate.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: All right, so Trump`s deadline to sell TikTok expires Wednesday, two days before Trump and Xi are set to discuss the final details. What are we expecting?\par \par \uc2 JO LING KENT: Yes, this is a great question for everyone on TikTok. It`s unclear what will happen, but experts do not expect the app to come down like it did back in mid-January.\par \par \uc2 Secretary Bessent says a deal would address U.S. National Security requirements, but keep Chinese characteristics of TikTok.\par \par \uc2 So, if a deal does fall through, a TikTok ban could impact roughly seven million small businesses who heavily rely on the platform, 170 million TikTok users here in the U.S. -- Nate.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Jo Ling, thank you.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: A federal appeals court late yesterday blocked President Trump from firing Federal Reserve Governor Lisa Cook. Now, the move clears away for Cook to participate in this week`s crucial two-day meeting on interest rates.\par \par \uc2 Last month, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , you may recall tried to remove her from the Board, alleging mortgage fraud, even though Cook has not been charged with a crime. Critics say the President`s push to remove her is a threat to the Fed`s independence.\par \par \uc2 Also late Monday, the Senate voted to confirm Stephen Miran, he is one of President Trump`s top economic advisers to serve on the Federal Board of Governors. He is also expected to vote at the Fed meeting.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Memphis, Tennessee could be the next city to see an influx of federal agents and National Guard troops, that`s according to the President himself. He says the effort is to crack down on violent crime, and like other cities sited by the administration, the mayor of Memphis is a Democrat.\par \par \uc2 Nicole Valdes is in Memphis with the reaction now to the President`s decision.\par \par \uc2 (Begin VT)\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP: We are sending in a lot of help.\par \par \uc2 NICOLE VALDES: President Trump mobilized federal law enforcement agents to deploy to the streets of Memphis on Monday. Trump says federal agents from multiple agencies including the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , \uc2 Drug Enforcement Administration\uc2 , and \uc2 Immigration and Customs Enforcement\uc2  will join \uc2 Tennessee National Guard\uc2  troops as part of a task force to combat crime in the city.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration has already deployed National Guard troops to the streets of Los Angeles and Washington, D.C. But Memphis will be the first city in a red state.\par \par \uc2 Many local Democratic officials are against the decision.\par \par \uc2 JUSTIN J. PEARSON (D) (State Representative): The militarized occupation of our city is not a resolution to the problems that we have.\par \par \uc2 NICOLE VALDES: A CBS News data team review of \uc2 FBI\uc2  statistics show that Memphis had the highest rate of violent crime of all major U.S. cities last year, but Memphis Police data shows there was a decrease in violent crime in the first nine months of this year.\par \par \uc2 MIKE MILLER\uc2  (Restaurant owner): We support our community.\par \par \uc2 NICOLE VALDES: \uc2 Mike Miller\uc2  has owned Patrick`s Restaurant in East Memphis for twenty years. He is optimistic a federal task force could help make the city safer.\par \par \uc2 MIKE MILLER\uc2 : It should make a difference. It should help. It should not be a negative.\par \par \uc2 NICOLE VALDES: Amber Sherman grew up here. The lifelong activist worries the presence of federal troops could do more harm than good.\par \par \uc2 AMBER SHERMAN (Activist): No one is really talking about the real root issues of crime and the fact that so much federal funding that has been cut from the city of Memphis that actually was working to combat crime.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 NICOLE VALDES: Now, this is not the only city that could see a federal law enforcement presence soon. The President yesterday threatened Chicago again, despite the opposition from that city`s Democratic mayor and governor.\par \par \uc2 And Gayle, another city the President mentioned yesterday, St. Louis.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: All right, Nicole, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 This morning, we`re learning about the results of new safety tests for popular electric vehicles. The \uc2 Insurance Institute for Highway Safety\uc2  looked at how seven E.V.s performed in collisions and avoiding pedestrians. Kris Van Cleave has got the results.\par \par \uc2 (Begin VT)\par \par \uc2 KRIS VAN CLEAVE: In tests simulating a crash between vehicles traveling in opposite directions at 40 miles an hour, four of the seven vehicles tested, the \uc2 BMW\uc2  i4, Chevy Blazer E.V., Tesla Cyber Truck, \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  ID. Buzz earned good ratings. The \uc2 Tesla\uc2  Model 3 earned a passing, acceptable, but two have room to improve.\par \par \uc2 The Nissan ARIYA SUV rated marginal, because the Insurance Institute for Highway Safety Injury Metrics showed a high risk of chest injuries to backseat passengers. And the Ford F-150 Lightning earned the lowest score, a poor rating because the rear seated dummy showed a high risk of chest, head, or neck injuries and the dummy`s lap belt moved from the ideal position on the pelvis vision on to the abdomen.\par \par \uc2 RAUL ARBELAEZ (\uc2 Insurance Institute for Highway Safety\uc2  vice president): That is not something we want to see in any crash.\par \par \uc2 KRIS VAN CLEAVE: \uc2 IIHS\uc2  Vice President Raul Arbelaez.\par \par \uc2 The common sensibility is a big vehicle, like a full size pickup should do well in a crash.\par \par \uc2 RAUL ARBELAEZ: Most people think bigger is better, heavier is better, and certainly we had that with the Ford F-150 Lightning. The vehicle structurally holds up really well in this crash, but fell short in protecting the rear seat position.\par \par \uc2 KRIS VAN CLEAVE: \uc2 IIHS\uc2  also looked at pedestrian crash avoidance technology, and most performed well. The \uc2 BMW\uc2 , Ford, and \uc2 Tesla\uc2  models all scored top marks joining the ARYA with good ratings.\par \par \uc2 When it 