ESON: Ahead, we have our "Dish" series. Tony takes us to a restaurant being praised for its modern grandma approach to cooking. Doesn`t that sound delicious? And Gayle is leaving. We`ll be right back.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: She doesn`t like the word Grandma.\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 (LOCAL NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (LOCAL WEATHER)\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 **********************************(08:00AM, EDT)**********************************\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: We welcome you back to CBS MORNINGS.\par \par \uc2 I`m Gayle King. That`s Tony Dokoupil. That`s Nate Burleson.\par \par \uc2 Coming up in this 8:00 hour, the stars of the new movie, "All of You" will be here. It`s a story with a twist about soul mates. Would you pay to find yours?\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Plus, our series, "The Dish" takes us to one of the top restaurants in the country. It happens to be in Cleveland. We`ll meet the chef who describes his cooking as modern grandma.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Best-selling author, Elin Hilderbrand stops by with her new writing partner, her daughter. We will hear about their first novel about a boarding school that is full of secrets.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: It has lots of secrets.\par \par \uc2 But first, here`s today`s "Eye Opener at 8:00."\par \par \uc2 Israel launches the main phase of its ground invasion of Gaza City while a U.N. Inquiry accuses top Israeli officials of committing genocide in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 DANIEL MERON: The report relies entirely on \uc2 Hamas\uc2  falsehoods, laundered and repeated by others.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: The suspect in the Charlie Kirk assassination appears before a judge later today. Investigators say he confessed online.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: President Trump says he ordered U.S. military forces to destroy another boat from Venezuela, claiming it was carrying illegal drugs to the U.S.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP: We have proof, all you have to do is 