s, I don`t know why. I didn`t get enough sleep.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: That`s all right.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: I turn it over to Mr. Burleson.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: All black people don`t look alike.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Come on, Gayle.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: This is Nate Burleson.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Are we going there at this hour of the morning? I got in late on a flight, all right.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Me, too.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Come on, brother. You`re talking chocolate versus butterscotch.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: I know. I know.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Two different flavors, Tony.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Mr. Burleson.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: All right, so Seattle professional athletes are a really close community, really like family.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: So this "Talk of the Table" is very close and near and dear to my heart.\par \par \uc2 So this is about former \uc2 NBA\uc2  player and three time dunk contest champion, Nate Robinson. He had a surprise reunion with the man who he says gave him the best gift he ever got.\par \par \uc2 Robinson was diagnosed with kidney disease in 2006 while he was still playing in the \uc2 NBA\uc2 , and then his kidneys failed in 2018. Last year, the basketball star announced on social media, and to all of his friends and family that he is looking for a kidney donor. He said that he was close to dying, and I know that for sure.\par \par \uc2 In February, a complete stranger gave Robinson a new kidney and a new lease on life. Yesterday, he shared this video of the two meeting again.\par \par \uc2 (Begin VT)\par \par \uc2 NATE ROBINSON (Former \uc2 NBA\uc2  player): Oh. Oh.\par \par \uc2 WOMAN: Oh my goodness.\par \par \uc2 NATE ROBINSON: Oh, my God. You guys surprised me today. Man, this is too much. (Bleep). Oh, my God.\par \par \uc2 By far the best present I ever got in my life. Literally, I cried for like, maybe, like three days, and I was just thankful I`ve got this guy right here to thank for that.\par \par \uc2 Some people don`t get to meet their guardian angels. He helped me out a lot, big time. Man, I was struggling, and he came through in the clutch.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: So Nate Robinson is one of the most gifted athletes to ever come out of Seattle, Washington, and he`s an even better man than an athlete.\par \par \uc2 I bring that up because when he was going through this, it was shocking to all of us who were so close to him that, for what it`s worth, his body was failing him.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Yes.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: And then he was able to get this new lease on life. Shout out to Shane Cleveland, that`s the man.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I was wondering what his name was.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: And he was searching for that kidney, and this man stepped up. So I want to highlight that, because we were all rooting for him, and we`re glad that he --\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: We`re all fragile, we`re all human, but when you see somebody who`s at the peak of physical athleticism --\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Yes.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: -- to struggle, it`s just so shocking and poignant.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I`m still thinking about Shane. Did he give it for -- a complete stranger.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Complete stranger.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I am blown away by that. Wow.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Complete stranger.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Wow.\par \par \uc2 My talk of the table has a basketball theme, too. It`s \uc2 L.A. Lakers\uc2  superstar Luka Doncic showing his team spirit and paying it forward in a big, big way.\par \par \uc2 Last month, an online fundraiser was created to help restore a mural of Lakers legend that would be the great Kobe Bryant and his daughter, Gigi. Now the mural showing the father and daughter who we all know were tragically killed in a helicopter crash in 2020 was defaced by graffiti. Who would do that?\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Right.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yesterday, Doncic made a $5,000.00 donation to cover the entire goal of the fundraiser. He said he feels it`s important to give back to the community that has given him so much.\par \par \uc2 The mural`s artist is Louis Palsino said this alone will have him in the hearts of everyone in Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 The other day at the Beyonce concert, Vanessa Bryant was there with her older daughter, Natalia. She`s stunningly beautiful, and it`s just so nice to see them out and about.\par \par \uc2 But you look at that mural and think, why in the world would somebody do that? That makes no sense whatsoever.\par \par \uc2 So the artist says this, he`s going to replace it. The mural has been untouched since 2020. He plans to now put a protective paint coat on the mural with the proceeds from the donations that are still pouring in.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: That`s great.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: But shoutout to Luka and shoutout to the artist.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: A small gesture from a guy who makes a ton of money, but that small gesture goes a long way.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes. Yes.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Yes. It does go a long way.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: People, leave the murals alone, especially that one.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Yes.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Sure.\par \par \uc2 All right, Tony, what have you got?\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Tony --\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: My "Talk of the Table." Some of the seemingly crazy ways we are apparently feeding baby animals in this country and around the world, this is from the Bronx Zoo. They`ve got a baby King Vulture, and rather than a grown vulture feeding it, they`ve got a zoo employee with a homemade vulture hand puppet -- the puppet rearing the vulture, which apparently is a decades old technique.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: What?\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Apparently -- they don`t want the vulture, the baby to imprint on a human, and, I guess, follow the employees` home. But it reminded me of the pandas. Remember these videos from a couple of years ago? They come out every now and then. Guys in panda suits.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: I mean, come on.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Come on.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: That`s ridiculous.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: That`s kind of ridiculous, right?\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Look at the size of that head.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: The pandas seem like they don`t know.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: It`s like the NBA Jam characters, man.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Are you kidding?\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: I mean, so we`ve been doing this around the world for years, and I mean, I think at some point we`re going to, like be able to read animal thoughts, and we`re going to find out they know the whole time. We`re not fooling these animals.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Yes, you`re right about that.\par \par \uc2 Oh my gosh, that is hilarious.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: But the babies are thriving.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: They are.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: But the babies are thriving.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: That`s the important thing.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Come on. Come on. Random dude in a costume.\par \par \uc2 All right, coming up next, Emmy winner, Samantha Bee is in the building. She`s actually in our progressive greenroom.\par \par \uc2 Coming up, she will talk about how she is being very outspoken and talking about something we don`t talk about enough, which is menopause.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Naturally, she turned that into a topic in her one-woman show.\par \par \uc2 Stick around. You`re going to love what`s coming up next. But first, here`s a check of your local weather.\par \par \uc2 (LOCAL WEATHER)\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: A whole lot of women.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: 