ou, John Legend.\par \par \uc2 JOHN LEGEND: Everybody is singing my song.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: I appreciate you.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: That`s good, Nate. That`s good.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: \uc2 Elizabeth Werner\uc2 , we appreciate you. We partner with all of these companies --\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Give us the greenlight.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: -- to get these deals.\par \par \uc2 To buy anything you saw, scan the QR code on your screen or visit CBSDeals.com.\par \par \uc2 We will be right back.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: John, you have so many --\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 (Clip from "Ted Lasso"/Apple TV+)\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: That is the great Brett Goldstein as Roy Kent on the Emmy- winning show "Ted Lasso." You know it. You love it, too.\par \par \uc2 Now, Goldstein is going clean shaven in the Apple TV+ show, oh, no "Shrinking" it is called. It stars Jason Segel as Jimmy, a therapist who is grieving the death of his wife who was killed by a drunk driver.\par \par \uc2 Now in season two, Brett Goldstein shows up as that driver. Wow. Here is Goldstein meeting with Jimmy`s daughter, played by Lukita Maxwell.\par \par \uc2 (Clip from "Shrinking"/Apple TV+)\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Oh man, and you, you should see what happens after that. That is such a powerful scene. You`re going to have to get to Episode Four to get it, but it`s good.\par \par \uc2 Brett Goldstein is here. He also, by the way, co-created "Shrinking." Bravo to you, Brett.\par \par \uc2 BRETT GOLDSTEIN ("Shrinking" actor): Oh, thanks.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: This show is so good. We fell in love with you with "Ted Lasso," but you`ve done many things other than those shows. But let`s just concentrate on "Shrinking" for just a second.\par \par \uc2 So you`re co-creator, you wrote the role, but they say you weren`t planning to play the role. I don`t believe you.\par \par \uc2 So you`re writing it for somebody else?\par \par \uc2 BRETT GOLDSTEIN: Yes,