ooms, Gayle. Fifteen bathrooms, you can find an open one.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes, lots of places to go. Yes.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: It`s a beautiful, beautiful, beautiful home that is in a forest preserve.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: But in 2012 he was like, you know what? I`m ready to sell this home. Nobody would buy it for more than a decade. It was just too Michael, I guess, and you didn`t want to renovate it. You couldn`t make it a museum because of regulations.\par \par \uc2 So on and on and on.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Look at that gym.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Finally, good news for Michael Jordan. We can`t announce that, according to "The \uc2 Chicago Tribune\uc2 " and "The Chicago Business Journal," an unknown buyer has come forward and entered a contract with Mr. Jordan to purchase this home.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: For how much? Is it something like 14 --\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: We don`t know the price. The price fell from $29 million to $21 million to 16 to 13.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: So he`s looking to sell.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Wow.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I heard, it went to 40, but you know, when you`re looking to buy a house, you always say, the real estate agent, well, how long has it been on the market? Because you think that could help you get a better price.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: They say, oh, 12 years. You think, I`m really going to get a good deal out of it.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: It is about 12 years. Yes.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Although you know interest rates got cut, so maybe there`s an opportunity for someone out there.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: It is a beautiful home.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: That`s right. Gayle, you`re up.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Oh, okay. My talk of the table is a special serenade. So imagine this, you`re going for a