e future victims.\par \par \uc2 And a day after this decision inadvertently posted early, the Supreme Court made it official. For now, federal law supersedes Idaho law and the state must allow emergency abortions when necessary to protect a pregnant woman`s health, part of a push by President Biden`s Attorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  to keep up the legal pressure on protecting abortion rights.\par \par \uc2 MERRICK GARLAND\uc2  (US Attorney General): The Justice Department will continue to use every available tool to ensure that women in every state have access to that care.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 JAN CRAWFORD: Now, the court will hand down more decisions today and then again on Monday. Of course, we`re still waiting on those two big ones involving former President Trump, immunity for his actions around January 6, and what possible charges he could face -- Nate.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Jan, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Millions of Americans will be on the move this morning for the Fourth of July holiday week.\par \par \uc2 AAA predicts a new record for the number of travelers, nearly 71 million during the period lasting until next Sunday, July 7th. That includes more than 16 million people hitting the road.\par \par \uc2 And if you`re flying today, the TSA, they anticipate that they will be screening more than three million passengers, that`s the most ever in one day.\par \par \uc2 Now if Kris Van Cleave was here, he would hit you with a smile, raises his eyebrow concern and say avoid the roads next Wednesday July 3rd and avoid everything on Sunday July 7th, because you will be stuck somewhere.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Yes, it is always the day I am out-of-milk that is like the main travel day. It sounds like a four-hour ride to the grocery store.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Yes.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Coming up, a new flashpoint in the separation of church and state. We`ll show you why one state superintendent is requiring public 