finitely, Angel Reese, but very happy for Caitlin Clark.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: This is huge.\par \par \uc2 NATALIE MORALES: Yes. Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Some marketing strategy.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: That`s right. It is.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: It is opening doors for more to come.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: That`s right.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Let`s see.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Exactly right.\par \par \uc2 NATALIE MORALES: Let`s see it trickle down to the others.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Hopefully. That`s what we`re hoping.\par \par \uc2 Okay, imagine this.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Imagine you`re cleaning out your attic. That`s a little tease, right? Imagine you`re cleaning out your attic, preparing to move out of your house and who could have thought?\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: And what do you find?\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: A guitar.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Oh.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: A guitar and imagine finding out that the guitar is a long lost 12-string of John Lennon, and it has been missing for more than half a century.\par \par \uc2 NATALIE MORALES: Wow.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: The family that found it is now putting it up for auction. Julien`s Auction calls it the most important Beatles guitar to ever come to market and predicts it would fetch more than $800,000.00 next month.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Wow.\par \par \uc2 NATALIE MORALES: Wow.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: The auction says Gordon Waller, who is a singer, who was very close -- friends with the Beatle gave it to a road manager.\par \par \uc2 Guys, you can hear it when you listen to the opening of "Norwegian Wood" or "Hey, you`ve got to hide your love away."\par \par \uc2 NATALIE MORALES: Wow.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: You hear that guitar playing. You hear it "Help."\par \par \uc2 So this is a hugely important guitar in just --\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING