ORDES: Inflation is one reason Jay is on the fence.\par \par \uc2 JAY WISSENTON: Back in the day, haircuts was about 25 bucks, 20 to 25 bucks. But now we`re up to 50 bucks now and a lot of people can`t pay that, they go like, oh, that`s too much. And they hurry up and walk out the shop.\par \par \uc2 NANCY CORDES: They were all turned off when Trump mocked Biden`s stutter this weekend.\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (Former President of the United States): Bring the country to-to-together.\par \par \uc2 NANCY CORDES: Should he stop doing that?\par \par \uc2 PATTI GRANGER: I think he should stop doing that, yes.\par \par \uc2 JAY WISSENTON: Yes. Some things about Trump he shouldn`t -- he shouldn`t be doing, that he should stop doing.\par \par \uc2 NANCY CORDES: Do you think he will?\par \par \uc2 BOBBI TATUM: No.\par \par \uc2 PATTI GRANGER: No.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 NANCY CORDES: President Biden heads from here to the battleground state of Michigan today while Vice President Harris is set to visit an abortion clinic in Minneapolis. It is believed to be the first time that a sitting president or vice president has done that and it shows just how important the issue of reproductive rights is to the Biden campaign.\par \par \uc2 In fact, just last year, the issue drove Democratic voters to the polls in a pivotal State Supreme Court race and the campaign believes it could do the same in this battleground state this November -- Vlad.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: All right, we`ll be watching. Nancy Cordes for us.\par \par \uc2 Nancy, thank you.\par \par \uc2 A jury in Michigan is deciding if the father of a convicted school gunman should also go to prison for the attack. James Crumbley is charged with involuntary manslaughter after his son killed four other students at his high school in 2021. Crumbley`s wife was convicted of similar charges at a separate trial last month.\par \par \uc2 Elaine Quijano reports on yesterday`s closing arguments.\par \par 