e cyberattack on the country`s biggest healthcare payment system. This one affects millions of Americans.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: I`m Vladimir Duthiers. I`ve got the story of a man once named World`s Best Bartender before nearly losing everything. It`s a tale of resilience and redemption.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: And we like those stories. But first, here`s today`s "Eye Opener at Eight."\par \par \uc2 (PROTESTERS chanting "Keep TikTok.")\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: A bill that could ban TikTok faces an uncertain future in the Senate after passing the House with bipartisan support.\par \par \uc2 REP. NANCY PELOSI (D-CA): This is not an attempt to ban TikTok. Its attempt to make TikTok better. Tic Tac Toe. A winner. A winner.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: A major winter storm moves through the Rockies hammering Colorado.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE ABRAMS: . where we could see up to three feet of snow in the Mile High City, a month`s worth could pile up. March is typically Denver`s snowiest month with 11-and-a-half inches.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: An explosion injures more than a dozen members of law enforcement at an \uc2 FBI\uc2  training facility in California.\par \par \uc2 SGT. FRANK GONZALEZ (Orange County Sheriff`s Department): It`s not a good feeling anytime an injury happens to anybody, including members of our own staff.\par \par \uc2 (PEOPLE cheering)\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: And Dallas Seavey wins the Iditarod Dog Sled Race in Alaska. He`s the first to win it six times, but he did not do it alone.\par \par \uc2 DALLAS SEAVEY (Iditarod Dog Sled Race six-time winner): The heart and soul of this sport is sled dogs. I don`t win Iditarod without a dog team.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: At least he`s honest.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Iditarod. The dogs are like Idita-what? Roo.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes, I am always fascinated by that.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: It`s amazing.\par \par \uc2 All right, we`re 