 experience across the United States.\par \par \uc2 (Begin VT)\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: You can find Jack McGarry doing way more than tending bar.\par \par \uc2 JACK MCGARRY (The Dead Rabbit): I`m not just doing this for you guys. This is what I do every day.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: At his pub, The Dead Rabbit in Lower Manhattan.\par \par \uc2 JACK MCGARRY: You probably didn`t think you`re sort of going to see arts and crafts I`d imagine.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: From painting walls, to trimming threads. No task is beneath the Belfast native who wanted to create an experience true to the pubs he knew growing up.\par \par \uc2 JACK MCGARRY: The pub is the heartbeat of a community. It is where you go to meet up, you go to talk, you go to have baptisms, bar mitzvahs, Irish Weeks, so when we came here, I wanted to show that an Irish pub can be both a haven for hospitality, but also excellence.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: McGarry moved to the US in 2012 and the accolades soon followed. At age 23, McGarry was the youngest ever person named International Bartender of the Year and his pub was named Best in the World.\par \par \uc2 JACK MCGARRY: When I was younger, my obsession was with becoming the best bartender in the world, literally, since I was 15 years old. A lot of people had pictures in their wall of -- are walls of Pamela Anderson. My walls were filled with bartenders.\par \par \uc2 I was like, I`m going to be that guy. I want to be the best bartender and the word.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: What was it for you that tipped you into a space you didn`t want to be in?\par \par \uc2 JACK MCGARRY: So, the fact that I got the thing that I wanted, and then realized that it was not fun anymore, like it`s a plate that sits on your mantelpiece, and that`s it. You`re completely unsure of what your purpose is.\par \par \uc2 Because after I got that, my love of bartending stopped.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: What earned him acclaim became a danger. Unable to find answers, he turned to alcohol and drugs.\par \par \uc2 JACK MCGARRY: I got to the point where like, I had to stop working for a while and then I tried to commit suicide towards the and I woke up in a hospital with my stomach pumped.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: In 2016, McGary, entered rehab and he shared his ongoing recovery on social media. In 2017, he announced his transition from bartending to operations. And in 2018, he wrote: "My hell is long gone, but not forgotten."\par \par \uc2 JACK MCGARRY: When I got out of rehab, nobody in this industry was really talking about mental health. I was like, I know I am going to lose some people, I`m going to lose money. Liquor brands won`t want to work with me and stuff like that. But I was like, so be it, if it helps one person, even just one person, I`ll have done my bit.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: The search for a healthier path involved trial and error.\par \par \uc2 JACK MCGARRY: I tried everything, \uc2 SoulCycle\uc2 , yoga. I got very, very impatient with yoga. And then I tried running and it just clicked.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: He now runs nearly every day, and has completed several marathons.\par \par \uc2 JACK MCGARRY: In a lot of ways I was running towards the discomfort, the pain, as opposed to previously with being in addiction and alcoholism, you`re running away from issues. At the end of the day, that`s the only way you`re going to grow.\par \par \uc2 The two big things that I would do are running and reading. Between the two of them, it`s a source of inspiration. It`s a source of pride and it ensures that you`re the best version of yourself when you turn up.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Today, he is doing a lot. Now married to his wife, Kati, and the father of three-year-old Lucas and one-year-old Tommy, he`s earned two degrees, and is overseeing a booming business.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER: Now boarding Flight 18.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: In September, McGarry launched the Irish Exit, a fast casual spot at Grand Central Terminal. And he`s also revamped the original Dead Rabbit with plans to expand the brand to other cities in the US.\par \par \uc2 JACK MCGARRY: The way I look at competition now, it is with me, I want to be the best version of me. But my purpose is much larger than a plate on a back bar, it`s being a brand ambassador for the country of Ireland.\par \par \uc2 I want to make sure that we bring up the next generation of that talent back home for the music, the art, the crafts, and I want to bring that version of Ireland to as many cities in America as I can.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: A lot of people will see this and say, wow, it must be doubly hard to be sober but you`re surrounded by alcohol and you`re surrounded by people drinking.\par \par \uc2 JACK MCGARRY: To me, it`s doubly easy because they get constant reinforcements of, this is something that`s not conducive with my life, but I still enjoy and love the magic of a bar room and the magic of the story that we`re telling in Ireland.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: So before we talk about The Dead Rabbit and Jack, if you or a loved one is in emotional distress, call or text the Suicide Crisis Lifeline at 988. Again, that number is 988.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I love this story, Vlad.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: His story is an incredible one and what he`s attempted to do with The Dead Rabbit and has succeeded is to change the image that we have in this country of what an Irish pub is, which is often inauthentic.\par \par \uc2 What he`s done here at The Dead Rabbit and why he`s won all of these accolades is, this is a true authentic Irish pub. He showcases Irish artists and Irish singers on a regular basis. The food is typically the fair, and it is typically Irish.\par \par \uc2 You really do get a sense that you`re in either in Dublin or in Belfast, wherever your favorite tipple spot is. That`s what you get when you`re at The Dead Rabbit.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: The irony though of being called the Best Bartender in the World, and then having that issue.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: And then falling into addiction.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes, and then turning that around.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Yes.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: And still working there and being there every day surrounded by this. He says it`s a struggle every day that all addicts understand. He`s able through his running, through the things that -- his family, and the things that he does and his outside pursuits to overcome that addiction, but it`s a struggle every day.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Every day, they call it alcohol-ism not wasm, that`s from the community, yes.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Exactly right.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: All right, Mr. McGarry.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Up next -- thank you very much. Up next, our CBS MORNINGS deals. Ashley Bellman will show us a little something you might want to add to your skincare routine. And yes, it`s at an exclusive low price.\par \par \uc2 We`ll be right back.\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Time now for \uc2 CBS\uc2  MORNINGS Deals. Today, we`ve got three products all available at exclusive discounts. To start shopping now scan the QR code on your screen or visit CBSDeals.com.\par \par \uc2 Lifestyle expert, Ashley Bellman joins us now.\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 ASHLEY BELLMAN (Lifestyle expert): Good morning. I am so excited to talk to you about all of these products, but I`m going to start with the Lancer Microdermabrasion Facial tool.\par \par \uc2 So feel this, this is going to suck out any dead skin leaving you --\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: And it doesn`t hurt.\par \par \uc2 ASHLEY BELLMAN: No, but it does have that diamond tip.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Everybody is like, let me try it.\par \par \uc2 ASHLEY BELLMAN: That`s going to exfoliate your skin