d remove the dog from the situation.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Right.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes. yes.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: And maybe get some training, which I`m told that they have done for Commander.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I`ll bet the Secret Service agents are going, why I ought to - -\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Right. Exactly.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: According to these e-mails and some of the quotes from the agents, I mean, they`ve got stitches, antibiotics.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Stitches --\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Yes.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: There was blood on the lobby floor for a while.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: It`s not good.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: They had to lay --\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Not good.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: It is good that he`s not there anymore.\par \par \uc2 All right, I got to show you all this incredible video that shows a train torpedoing an Amazon truck and splitting it in half.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: What?\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: That driver, folks, lucky to survive.\par \par \uc2 In November, 2021, Alexander Evans was driving down a road outside Milwaukee. Dashcam video newly obtained by TMZ shows the train slamming through his vehicle. Wait for it. Here it comes.\par \par \uc2 You see the train in the background there?\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Whoa. Vlad.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Crushing the back half.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Watch this again.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Oh, my gosh.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Look at Mr. Evans, though.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: That`s a train.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: At one point, he just looks behind him and he goes, man, I`m having a day.\par \par \uc2 Evans told the local station that he is deaf in his left ear and did not hear the train`s horn in time. He also said there were no signals or lights to warn him about the oncoming danger.\par \par