led so early, whether it`s for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  or not for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . I just want people to have the opportunity to vote and think that your vote still makes a difference. And we`re calling it now.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Speaking as -- last thing quickly, what does Biden do?\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: We`re not.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes, we are not.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: If you`re telling us that information right now, what does Biden do moving forward?\par \par \uc2 TERRY SULLIVAN: Look, he`s got to focus on the general election. This is now a general election campaign. And America`s going to have a choice, and they`ve got quite a few months to figure this thing out between those two candidates. If you`re happy with the way \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has done things, you`re going to vote for him. If you`re unhappy, you`re going to vote for Trump.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Longest general election we`ve ever had.\par \par \uc2 TERRY SULLIVAN: Yep.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Yep.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: So you think \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  should drop out?\par \par \uc2 TERRY SULLIVAN: Yes. I mean, but like, she`s going to run out of money. Her donors are going to stop giving her money. And that`s -- people only stop running for president for one reason. They don`t -- not that they think they`re no longer smart enough or qualified. It`s they run out of money.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: It`s the money.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Well, she says she`s not going to. We`ll see. But you`re right. Everybody says I`m not going to and then the next hour. It`s like, I`m out.\par \par \uc2 TERRY SULLIVAN: They also say they`re not going to be vice president. They`re not interested until they`re picked.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yes.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Oh, you`ve been watching the show.\par \par \uc2 TERRY SULLIVAN: Oh yes.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Thank you, Terry Sullivan.\par \par \uc2 TERRY SULLIVAN: Good questions.\par \par \