he details of what is a stunning medical breakthrough.\par \par \uc2 You`re watching CBS MORNINGS.\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Here in New York, \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  testified yesterday in the civil court trial to determine the Trump organization`s liability for fraud.\par \par \uc2 Attorneys asked the former president`s daughter if she knowingly passed along misleading business documents while she served as an executive in the family business.\par \par \uc2 Scott MacFarlane was in the court for the hearing.\par \par \uc2 Scott, what do you know?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT MACFARLANE: Hey, Nate. Good morning.\par \par \uc2 The tone and the tenor of \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  was just so different from her father`s outbursts and flashes of anger earlier this week. She spoke in a voice so soft and quiet, the judge frequently asked her to speak up and into the microphone at least four times.\par \par \uc2 (Begin VT)\par \par \uc2 SCOTT MACFARLANE: \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  became the fourth and final member of her family to take the stand in the New York civil fraud trial against the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: How are you doing, Ivanka?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT MACFARLANE: Under questioning as a witness, not a defendant, she frequently told the state attorney, "I don`t recall" and insisted several times she didn`t prepare her father`s financial statements as she said in a deposition last summer.\par \par \uc2 IVANKA TRUMP (Donald Trump`s daughter): I`ve never prepared one. I don`t know. I`ve never made one. I`m not an accountant.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT MACFARLANE: She left the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  in 2017 when her father became president, but the New York Attorney General`s Office says she was there and talking to lenders during the time the company landed sweetheart loans by exaggerating Trump`s worth.\par \par \uc2 LETITIA JAMES (New York attorney general): She was enriched and clearly, you cannot distance yourself from that fact. The documents do not lie.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT MACFARLANE: E-mails revealed in court showed her involvement on the financing for the Doral Golf Club in Florida in 2011. And she was copied on a submission to \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  of her father`s statement of financial conditions, which portrayed his net worth is $3 billion higher than it actually was that was.\par \par \uc2 That resulted in a deal with much better loan rates that had previously been offered. She then wrote to her fellow executives, "It doesn`t get better than this."\par \par \uc2 WOMAN: She wanted to get in and out as unscathed as possible with doing as little damage as possible to her brothers and her father. I think she did just that.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 SCOTT MACFARLANE: \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  was New York state`s final witness. Lawyers for former President Trump`s business begin making their case next.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: She looked very confident, Scott, walking in that courtroom, no bag with her, nobody around her. She -- in many ways it looked like she was walking on a runway.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: I`m seeing it like it`s a runway.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: So how did she come across in the courtroom, do you think to the judge?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT MACFARLANE: It was striking because it was so subtle. It was a whisper at times. The judge told her to speak up and get into the microphone because we can`t hear you.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Was that strategy, do you think?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT MACFARLANE: It certainly was effective. If it was, she was supposed to be back there today, instead, they cut her off yesterday afternoon, sent her home, said they`re done.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: She seemed confident. The state also seemed confident. You have expected them to produce the champagne cork from when they celebrated the deal.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Right.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: I do not recall that champagne.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: I